From: Tabor SPE toolchain project
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] rs6000: address SPE PIC caller LR through argument pointer

Local candidate against checksum-pinned GCC8.5.0, not an upstream backport.
The reduced probe faults with -fpic -fstack-protector-strong under both libc
runtimes. The generated backchain load addresses SP+64 instead of SP+0.
Use the argument pointer, whose elimination offset names the incoming frame,
to load its saved LR directly. Restrict to SPE/ABI_V4/count0 PIC; retain all
other target behavior and stack protection. Runtime validation pending.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.c
@@ -25497,5 +25497,15 @@
       cfun->machine->ra_needs_full_frame = 1;
 
+      /* The incoming argument frame names the caller's saved LR even when
+         stack protection moves the local frame origin.  Do not derive it
+         from the local backchain address for SPE PIC.  */
+      if (count == 0 && TARGET_SPE && DEFAULT_ABI == ABI_V4)
+        {
+          rtx addr = plus_constant (Pmode, arg_pointer_rtx,
+                                    RETURN_ADDRESS_OFFSET);
+          return gen_rtx_MEM (Pmode, memory_address (Pmode, addr));
+        }
+
       if (count == 0)
 	/* FRAME is set to frame_pointer_rtx by the generic code, but that
 	   is good for loading 0(r1) only when !FRAME_GROWS_DOWNWARD.  */
